        "This central theoretical claim — that not just exposure but exposure conditioned by absorptive capacity is the best conceptualisation of sectoral AI resilience — draws on aspects of both the task-based automation literature (Autor et al., 2003; Bessen, 2019) and dynamic-capabilities theory (Teece et al., 1997; Zahra & George, 2002), although the two are rarely integrated in this way. This paper poses rather than answers the empirical question of whether or not the conditioning relationship holds with a specific attenuating form given here (P5). A second, more modest theoretical contribution is that the argument of the societal consequence as constitutive, not incidental to —investedor users’ notion of sustainable adoption is a positioning setting apart how this framework has been applied from Kittipanya-ngam et al. and governance-led use of the same term (2025) and associated but different frameworks.",
